cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use RTsegmentator 1.0.0, cite this software by version and by the DOI
  archived for its release. Contours come from third-party models: also cite each
  model's own publication and respect its licence, as listed in EXTERNAL_MODELS.md
  and in the rtsegmentator_manifest.json of every result package.
title: "RTsegmentator: a DICOM RT segmentation portal and API"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - name: RTsegmentator contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/kstawiski/rtsegmentator
url: https://kstawiski.github.io/rtsegmentator/
abstract: >-
  RTsegmentator is a web portal and versioned REST API that runs open
  segmentation models on uploaded DICOM CT, MR and PET series and returns DICOM
  RTSTRUCT contours. Before export, each mask is mapped directly onto the source
  image grid and checked by a contour-to-mask round trip against the referenced
  images. Every result package carries a manifest that lists the model, its
  licence and limitations, the exact ROI names written, the source series and a
  SHA-256 checksum for each file. A standard-library Python client submits
  series in batch and verifies downloaded packages; RTpipeline imports the
  verified packages as a segmentation source for dose-volume and radiomics
  analysis.
keywords:
  - radiotherapy
  - DICOM RT
  - RTSTRUCT
  - auto-segmentation
  - medical image segmentation
  - deep learning
  - research software
